# Testing Strategy

## TDD Workflow (Mandatory)

1. **RED** — Write a failing test first
2. **GREEN** — Write minimal code to pass
3. **REFACTOR** — Clean up while tests stay green

**No implementation without tests first.**

## Vitest Configuration (Recommended)

```typescript
// vitest.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";
import path from "node:path";

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    globals: true,
    environment: "node",
    include: ["src/**/*.test.ts", "src/**/*.spec.ts"],
    coverage: {
      provider: "v8",
      reporter: ["text", "json", "html"],
      exclude: ["node_modules", "dist", "**/*.d.ts", "**/*.test.ts"],
    },
    setupFiles: ["./src/test/setup.ts"],
  },
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      "@": path.resolve(__dirname, "./src"),
    },
  },
});
```

## Test Structure (AAA Pattern)

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from "vitest";
import { UserService } from "./user.service";
import { UserRepository } from "./user.repository";

describe("UserService", () => {
  let userService: UserService;
  let userRepository: UserRepository;

  beforeEach(() => {
    userRepository = {
      findById: vi.fn(),
      save: vi.fn(),
      existsByEmail: vi.fn(),
    } as unknown as UserRepository;

    userService = new UserService(userRepository);
  });

  describe("createUser", () => {
    it("should create user when email is unique", async () => {
      // Arrange
      const request = { email: "test@example.com", name: "Test User" };
      vi.mocked(userRepository.existsByEmail).mockResolvedValue(false);
      vi.mocked(userRepository.save).mockResolvedValue({
        id: "user-123",
        ...request,
      });

      // Act
      const result = await userService.createUser(request);

      // Assert
      expect(result.isSuccess).toBe(true);
      expect(result.data).toEqual({
        id: "user-123",
        email: "test@example.com",
        name: "Test User",
      });
      expect(userRepository.save).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
        expect.objectContaining({ email: "test@example.com" })
      );
    });

    it("should return failure when email already exists", async () => {
      // Arrange
      const request = { email: "existing@example.com", name: "Test User" };
      vi.mocked(userRepository.existsByEmail).mockResolvedValue(true);

      // Act
      const result = await userService.createUser(request);

      // Assert
      expect(result.isSuccess).toBe(false);
      expect(result.error?.code).toBe("EMAIL_EXISTS");
      expect(userRepository.save).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
    });
  });
});
```

## Naming Convention

```
{methodName}_should{expectedBehavior}_when{condition}
```

Examples:
- `createUser_shouldReturnSuccess_whenEmailIsUnique`
- `createUser_shouldReturnFailure_whenEmailExists`
- `findById_shouldReturnUndefined_whenUserNotFound`

Or use descriptive strings in `it()`:
- `it("should create user when email is unique")`
- `it("should return failure when email already exists")`

## Mocking with Vitest

```typescript
import { vi, describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach } from "vitest";

// Mock a module
vi.mock("./user.repository", () => ({
  UserRepository: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    findById: vi.fn(),
    save: vi.fn(),
  })),
}));

// Mock a function
const mockFetch = vi.fn();
vi.stubGlobal("fetch", mockFetch);

// Spy on existing function
const logSpy = vi.spyOn(console, "log");

// Mock timers
beforeEach(() => {
  vi.useFakeTimers();
});

afterEach(() => {
  vi.useRealTimers();
});

it("should timeout after 5 seconds", async () => {
  const promise = someAsyncOperation();
  vi.advanceTimersByTime(5000);
  await expect(promise).rejects.toThrow("Timeout");
});
```

## HTTP Testing with Supertest

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterAll } from "vitest";
import request from "supertest";
import { createApp } from "./app";
import type { Express } from "express";

describe("User API", () => {
  let app: Express;

  beforeAll(() => {
    app = createApp();
  });

  describe("GET /api/users/:id", () => {
    it("should return user when found", async () => {
      const response = await request(app)
        .get("/api/users/user-123")
        .expect("Content-Type", /json/)
        .expect(200);

      expect(response.body).toEqual({
        id: "user-123",
        email: "test@example.com",
        name: "Test User",
      });
    });

    it("should return 404 when user not found", async () => {
      const response = await request(app)
        .get("/api/users/non-existent")
        .expect(404);

      expect(response.body).toMatchObject({
        status: 404,
        title: "Not Found",
      });
    });
  });

  describe("POST /api/users", () => {
    it("should create user with valid data", async () => {
      const response = await request(app)
        .post("/api/users")
        .send({ email: "new@example.com", name: "New User" })
        .expect("Content-Type", /json/)
        .expect(201);

      expect(response.body).toMatchObject({
        email: "new@example.com",
        name: "New User",
      });
      expect(response.body.id).toBeDefined();
    });

    it("should return 400 for invalid email", async () => {
      const response = await request(app)
        .post("/api/users")
        .send({ email: "invalid-email", name: "Test" })
        .expect(400);

      expect(response.body.errors).toBeDefined();
    });
  });
});
```

## Integration Tests with Testcontainers

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterAll } from "vitest";
import { PostgreSqlContainer, StartedPostgreSqlContainer } from "@testcontainers/postgresql";
import { PrismaClient } from "@prisma/client";

describe("UserRepository Integration", () => {
  let container: StartedPostgreSqlContainer;
  let prisma: PrismaClient;

  beforeAll(async () => {
    // Start PostgreSQL container
    container = await new PostgreSqlContainer("postgres:16-alpine")
      .withDatabase("testdb")
      .withUsername("test")
      .withPassword("test")
      .start();

    // Configure Prisma with container URL
    process.env.DATABASE_URL = container.getConnectionUri();
    prisma = new PrismaClient();

    // Run migrations
    await prisma.$executeRaw`CREATE TABLE users (
      id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
      email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
      name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
      created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
    )`;
  }, 60000); // 60s timeout for container startup

  afterAll(async () => {
    await prisma.$disconnect();
    await container.stop();
  });

  it("should save and retrieve user", async () => {
    // Arrange
    const userData = { email: "test@example.com", name: "Test User" };

    // Act
    const created = await prisma.user.create({ data: userData });
    const found = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { id: created.id } });

    // Assert
    expect(found).toMatchObject(userData);
    expect(found?.id).toBe(created.id);
  });

  it("should enforce unique email constraint", async () => {
    // Arrange
    await prisma.user.create({
      data: { email: "duplicate@example.com", name: "User 1" },
    });

    // Act & Assert
    await expect(
      prisma.user.create({
        data: { email: "duplicate@example.com", name: "User 2" },
      })
    ).rejects.toThrow();
  });
});
```

## Testing with MSW (Mock Service Worker)

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterAll, afterEach } from "vitest";
import { setupServer } from "msw/node";
import { http, HttpResponse } from "msw";
import { UserApiClient } from "./user-api-client";

const server = setupServer(
  http.get("https://api.example.com/users/:id", ({ params }) => {
    const { id } = params;
    if (id === "not-found") {
      return new HttpResponse(null, { status: 404 });
    }
    return HttpResponse.json({
      id,
      email: "test@example.com",
      name: "Test User",
    });
  }),

  http.post("https://api.example.com/users", async ({ request }) => {
    const body = await request.json();
    return HttpResponse.json({ id: "new-user", ...body }, { status: 201 });
  })
);

beforeAll(() => server.listen({ onUnhandledRequest: "error" }));
afterAll(() => server.close());
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());

describe("UserApiClient", () => {
  const client = new UserApiClient("https://api.example.com");

  it("should fetch user by id", async () => {
    const user = await client.getUser("user-123");
    expect(user).toEqual({
      id: "user-123",
      email: "test@example.com",
      name: "Test User",
    });
  });

  it("should handle not found", async () => {
    await expect(client.getUser("not-found")).rejects.toThrow("User not found");
  });

  it("should create user", async () => {
    const user = await client.createUser({
      email: "new@example.com",
      name: "New User",
    });
    expect(user.id).toBe("new-user");
  });
});
```

## Parameterized Tests

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from "vitest";

describe("validateEmail", () => {
  it.each([
    ["test@example.com", true],
    ["user.name@domain.org", true],
    ["invalid-email", false],
    ["@nodomain.com", false],
    ["", false],
  ])('validateEmail("%s") should return %s', (email, expected) => {
    expect(validateEmail(email)).toBe(expected);
  });

  it.each`
    email                  | valid    | reason
    ${"test@example.com"}  | ${true}  | ${"standard email"}
    ${"invalid"}           | ${false} | ${"missing @"}
    ${"@example.com"}      | ${false} | ${"missing local part"}
  `('$email should be $valid ($reason)', ({ email, valid }) => {
    expect(validateEmail(email)).toBe(valid);
  });
});
```

## Test Fixtures and Factories

```typescript
// test/factories/user.factory.ts
import { faker } from "@faker-js/faker";
import type { User, CreateUserRequest } from "@/modules/users/user.types";

export function createUserRequest(
  overrides?: Partial<CreateUserRequest>
): CreateUserRequest {
  return {
    email: faker.internet.email(),
    name: faker.person.fullName(),
    ...overrides,
  };
}

export function createUser(overrides?: Partial<User>): User {
  return {
    id: faker.string.uuid(),
    email: faker.internet.email(),
    name: faker.person.fullName(),
    createdAt: faker.date.past(),
    ...overrides,
  };
}

// Usage in tests
it("should create user", async () => {
  const request = createUserRequest({ email: "specific@example.com" });
  const result = await userService.createUser(request);
  expect(result.data?.email).toBe("specific@example.com");
});
```

## Test Configuration

```typescript
// src/test/setup.ts
import { beforeAll, afterAll, afterEach } from "vitest";
import { vi } from "vitest";

// Reset mocks after each test
afterEach(() => {
  vi.clearAllMocks();
});

// Global test setup
beforeAll(() => {
  // Set test environment variables
  process.env.NODE_ENV = "test";
  process.env.LOG_LEVEL = "silent";
});

// Global cleanup
afterAll(() => {
  vi.restoreAllMocks();
});
```

## Test Quality Standards

- Tests MUST be deterministic and isolated
- Tests MUST NOT depend on execution order
- Mock external dependencies in unit tests
- Use Testcontainers for real database in integration tests
- Aim for meaningful coverage, not arbitrary percentages
- Each test should test ONE behavior
- Use descriptive test names
- Keep tests simple and readable

## Coverage Requirements

```typescript
// vitest.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    coverage: {
      statements: 80,
      branches: 80,
      functions: 80,
      lines: 80,
      exclude: [
        "**/*.d.ts",
        "**/index.ts", // barrel exports
        "**/types/**",
        "**/test/**",
      ],
    },
  },
});
```

## Conventions

- Unit tests: Test individual components in isolation with mocks
- Integration tests: Test interactions with database using Testcontainers
- E2E tests: Test full request/response cycle with Supertest
- Use Vitest for modern, fast testing (preferred over Jest)
- Use MSW for mocking external HTTP calls
- ALWAYS clean up test data between tests
- Mock time-dependent code (use `vi.useFakeTimers()`)
- Run tests in CI on every push

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Writing tests after implementation
- ❌ Testing implementation details instead of behavior
- ❌ Sharing state between tests
- ❌ Using real external services in unit tests
- ❌ Ignoring flaky tests
- ❌ Testing private methods directly
- ❌ Overly complex test setup
- ❌ Not testing error cases

**See also:** `error-handling.mdc`, `controllers.mdc`, `orm.mdc`
